## 1. Security Checks by Architectural Boundary (`SR5`–`SR10`)

Cross-reference the workspace's safe implementation patterns in {{secure_coding_link}}:

| Boundary & Rule | What to Inspect in the Diff | Safe Pattern Requirement | Read-Only Scan / Verification Command |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Input, Injection & Deserialization (`SR5`)** | Dynamic SQL/command/path construction, unsafe deserialization, or request schemas missing unknown-field rejection | Parameterized queries only; strict DTO validation (`extra="forbid"` or equivalent); no `eval`/`exec`/`pickle`/`shell=True` | `rg -n "{{injection_sink_pattern}}" {{target_dir}}` |
| **Client & UI Boundary (`SR6`)** | Raw HTML/DOM injection, unvalidated redirect targets, plaintext token storage, or missing WebSocket `Origin` check | Context-aware escaping, allow-listed redirects, secure credential storage, and server-side guard enforcement | `rg -n "{{client_sink_pattern}}" {{target_dir}}` |
| **Secrets, PII & Error Envelopes (`SR7`)** | Hardcoded API keys/passwords/tokens in code/fixtures, or PII/stack traces leaked in logs and error responses | Secrets loaded from environment/secret manager only; structured error envelope without internal details | `{{secret_scan_cmd}}` |
| **Outbound Network & File Handling (`SR8`)** | User-influenced URLs passed to HTTP clients (SSRF), missing timeouts, or unvalidated file uploads/paths | Host/scheme allow-list, private IP block, explicit timeout, `Path.resolve()` containment, upload size & MIME validation | `rg -n "{{outbound_file_pattern}}" {{target_dir}}` |
| **Supply-Chain & Dependencies (`SR9`)** | Added or upgraded packages in dependency manifests / lockfiles | Justified need, pinned lockfile entry, zero known exploitable vulnerabilities | `{{dependency_audit_cmd}}` |
| **Cryptography & Auth Flows (`SR10`)** | Token generation, password hashing, webhook signature checks, session expiration/revocation | CSPRNG (`secrets`), platform crypto, constant-time digest comparison (`hmac.compare_digest`), bounded token TTL | `rg -n "{{weak_crypto_pattern}}" {{target_dir}}` |

