## 3. Deterministic CLI Verification Gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`)

All automated checks report strictly **`PASS`** or **`FAIL`** (`shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md`; `NOT_RUN`, `BLOCKED`, and `UNVERIFIED` never count as `PASS`):

| Gate | Command | `PASS` Criterion | `FAIL` Classification |
|---|---|---|---|
| **G1 — Injection & Unsafe Deserialization Scan (`SR5`)** | `rg -n "{{injection_sink_pattern}}" {{target_dir}}` | `0` unapproved matches | `BLOCKER` if reachable by untrusted input |
| **G2 — Secret & Credential Leak Scan (`SR7`)** | `{{secret_scan_cmd}}` | Exit `0` (`0` leaked secrets) | `BLOCKER` on any committed/staged secret |
| **G3 — Supply-Chain Advisory Audit (`SR9`)** | `{{dependency_audit_cmd}}` | Exit `0` (`0` exploitable advisories) | `BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` depending on reachability |
| **G4 — Auth & Tenant Isolation Suite (`SR3`, `SR4`)** | `{{auth_test_cmd}}` | Exit `0` — all `401`/`403`/`404` scope tests pass | `BLOCKER` on failing access-control test |

See [`references/01-triggers-threat-model-and-auth-matrix.md`]({{ref_01}}) for the authorization matrix and [`references/03-findings-verdict-and-report.md`]({{ref_03}}) for finding severity grading and report formatting.
